    "id": "rate_half_kb_m2_r4_coordinate_negative_loop_stratified_q_compiler",
    "title": "KoalaBear m2 r4 coordinate negative loop-stratified q compiler",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "exact square common-K q determinants of sizes five, four, and three in the negative loop strata",
    "statement": "For a negative packet with ell=0,1,2 antipodal common-K fibers, their locator R_Lambda divides A_1. Writing A_1=R_Lambda C, the 5-ell nonloop q equations form a square (5-ell)-by-(5-ell) matrix in the 3-ell coefficients of C and two coefficients of B_2. Its determinant must vanish and its kernel must keep B_2 nonzero on all K. Thus the two-loop rows reduce to explicit 3 x 3 signed determinants. This is a compiler, not a skeleton or orientation deletion.",
